  "id": "COMPOUND:19069 - PROTEIN:518",
  "verbalization": "Scillarenin 3-O-rhamnoside is implicated in the target pathway of Protein-arginine deiminase type-3, which in turn is targeted by multiple compounds, including 7-Methoxy-8-(4-Methylfuran-3-Yl)Chromen-2-One and 1,1,2-Trimethyl-3,5-bis(1-methylethenyl)cyclohexane. These compounds are linked to Protein-arginine deiminase type-1 through a series of intermediate targets, suggesting a potential mechanism where Scillarenin 3-O-rhamnoside may influence the activity of Protein-arginine deiminase type-1 via a chain of interactions. The evidence suggests that Scillarenin 3-O-rhamnoside could act as a modulator of this enzyme, possibly through a direct or indirect interaction that leads to the activation or inhibition of Protein-arginine deiminase type-1. The recurring involvement of Protein-arginine deiminase type-3 as a target and its subsequent connection to Protein-arginine deiminase type-1 implies a possible regulatory pathway, though the exact mechanism of action remains to be elucidated.",
